CloudBurrow patch 32 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1409). Applies after patch 0031.

The gap: googlesqlite_round_decimal (patch 0031) rounds a top-level
NUMERIC or BIGNUMERIC column's value; a parameterized NUMERIC(P, S) field
of a STRUCT column, an element of an ARRAY<NUMERIC(P, S)> column and a
field of an ARRAY<STRUCT<...>> column are kept at their full scale, and
one with more than P digits is kept. BigQuery rounds them by the field's
roundingMode, as a top-level column's
(https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/schemas#rounding_mode,
https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/data-types#parameterized_decimal_type).

The patch adds the SQLite function googlesqlite_round_decimal_nested(v,
spec): v, a STRUCT or ARRAY value as googlesqlite stores it (base64 of
its JSON layout), decoded, each value spec names rounded as
googlesqlite_round_decimal rounds one, at any depth, and encoded again;
OUT_OF_RANGE past a field's precision. spec is JSON: {"n": path, "p":
precision, "s": scale, "m": mode} for a decimal, {"f": {field: spec}}
for a STRUCT; an ARRAY's elements take the ARRAY's spec. The emulator
(its patch 0021) calls it from the column's triggers.
round_decimal_nested_test.go fails without the patch and passes with it.

